MERGED glm-53-flash
Single arm, 320 lines, 7 tests, clippy 0.

The branch the harness has never had. task_contract names three verification
kinds -- DeterministicTests, Benchmark, ReviewerJudgement -- and nothing branched
on it, so the only gate that existed was cargo.

Probed all eight pairings rather than trusting the suite:

  Tests kind  + Tests ev    Yes("cleared: 9 tests passed")
  Tests kind  + Bench ev    Mismatched { declared: DeterministicTests, got: "a benchmark score" }
  Tests kind  + Review ev   Mismatched
  Bench kind  + Bench ev    Yes("cleared benchmark: speedup 2.5 over 30 trials")
  Bench kind  + Tests ev    Mismatched { declared: Benchmark, got: "a build-and-test verdict" }
  Review kind + Review ev   Yes("cleared: the reviewer approved")
  Review kind + Tests ev    Mismatched
  Tests kind  + NoTests     No("not cleared: no test executed, and the gate requires at least one")

The last two lines are the task. Mismatched is a HARNESS fault -- we handed the
wrong instrument's output to the wrong gate -- and must never be recorded against
an arm. No is a candidate failure. An implementation returning No for everything
it cannot clear passes every other clause and silently blames arms for our bugs.

This is the blocker from farmerbob-p172. It does not finish KernelBench: a scorer
that RUNS a benchmark and feeds task_contract::score still does not exist, and
crossx is still 17 cargo references. But the verdict layer can now express a
benchmark result at all, which it could not before.
